# Every pull request automatically requests a review from the owner listed here.
#
# GitHub never requests a review from the PR's own author, so your own pull
# requests will not show a request from you — that is the rule working, not a
# broken file. It takes effect for pull requests opened against a branch that
# already has this file, so it starts working once it is on main.
#
# A single catch-all is deliberate: with one maintainer, per-directory rules
# would all resolve to the same person and only add noise. Split it when there
# is someone else to split it with.

